Researchers in Leicester are celebrating the completion of recruitment to the MINT-COPD trial after the 80th and final participant was seen this week.

The achievement marks an important milestone for the study, which is being delivered through the #NIHRBRCLeiecster at @Leic_hospital and seeks to improve recovery and quality of life for people living with #COPD following a hospital admission.

MINT-COPD (Maintaining the Integrity of Muscle Trial in Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease) is investigating whether a novel treatment, known as RJx-01, can help preserve muscle health and improve recovery for people hospitalised with severe flare-ups of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). 

COPD is a major cause of ill health worldwide, and hospital admissions can result in significant loss of muscle strength and physical function, affecting patients’ independence and quality of life.

